  "note": "Read-only suite, safe to re-run. Every occupancy case isolates ONE position with `search` first, so nothing depends on row order - a suite that assumed positions.0 was a particular position would pass today and go flaky the moment another position is added. Filter cases added 2026-09-08: this list filters in TWO places - positionCode and name narrow in storage, while occupancy, personName, titleName and employeeId only exist after the fold, so leaves on them are evaluated there. The split is only sound under an AND, which is why an OR across the two kinds is refused rather than answered wrong. The occupancy pair asserts a complement so it cannot be fooled by the fixture count.",
